description:
Fundamental of surveying and evolution from chain, compass,theodolite , total station( to digital and UAV-based surveying methods, introduction to modern instrumentation: GNSS, UAVs, LiDAR;
Geodesy and GNSS/GPS Surveying(GPS principles, satellite geometry, datums (WGS84, UTM), and use in surveying);
Introduction to Remote Sensing;Photogrammetry and UAV Applications;
Drone types (multirotor, fixed-wing), payloads (RGB, LiDAR), flight planning (GSD, overlap), and DGCA regulations in India;
GIS and Spatial Data Integration;Image overlap, structure-from-motion (SfM) concept, generation of orthomosaics and DEMs (conceptual only);
Combining GNSS, RGB, and LiDAR data; case studies – topographic mapping, construction monitoring, landslide/flood mapping;
Applications of Surveying and Remote Sensing in Civil Engineering Infrastructure Planning and Construction; Emerging Geospatial Technologies;
